      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When shipping a motorcycle to or from Kalpi, the paperwork you prepare will determine how smoothly the consignment passes through customs and local authorities. Below is a concise checklist of the essential documents you must assemble and the key points that can prevent delays or penalties.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self‑attested RC Photocopy</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The original Registration Certificate (RC) must be photocopied, and the copy needs to be self‑attested by the owner or a notary. This proves ownership and allows the transporter to verify the bike’s legal identity. Without this, customs officials can refuse to release the vehicle.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate must be valid at the time of transit. A fresh certificate is required for all vehicles moving between states. An expired PUC can lead to fines and even impoundment of the bike.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A comprehensive insurance policy that covers the bike for the entire journey is mandatory. The policy should be in force from the point of departure to the point of arrival, and the insurer’s details must be clearly stated on the certificate.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The International Bilateral Agreement (IBA) requires that the consignment bilty be issued by an authorized transporter. The bilty must include the bike’s details (make, model, chassis number), consignor and consignee information, and the agreed freight charges.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>An IBA‑approved bilty guarantees that the shipment is recognized by maritime and inland transport authorities</span>
  </li>
</ul>
  </div>
</div>

<p>One of the most critical aspects of marine transit insurance for motorcycles is the <strong>100% Declared‑Value Coverage</strong>. This type of policy ensures that the insurer will pay the full declared value of the bike in the event of loss, theft, or damage during transit.</p>
<p>Unlike partial coverage plans, a 100% declared‑value policy protects the owner from having to prove the exact value at the time of loss, thereby speeding up the claim process and reducing administrative hassle.</p>

<p>To sum up, the four core documents—self‑attested RC photocopy, current PUC certificate, valid insurance certificate, and IBA‑approved consignment bilty—form the backbone of a compliant bike transportation shipment in Kalpi. Coupled with a 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance, these documents safeguard your investment and ensure a hassle‑free delivery from start to finish.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Kalpi</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a Two‑Wheeler or Motorcycle arrives at its destination, the handover process must be meticulous to ensure both parties agree on the vehicle’s condition and mileage.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The delivery team follows a three‑step protocol that includes daylight re‑inspection, odometer verification, and a signed condition sign‑off.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Each step is documented on the same day to preserve accuracy and prevent disputes.</span></li></ul>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Daylight Condition Re‑Inspection</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The delivery driver or agent conducts a visual check of the motorcycle in natural daylight, which eliminates shadows and highlights any new dents, scratches, or fluid leaks that were not apparent in the original pickup photos.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>The agent compares the current condition to the high‑resolution images captured at pickup, noting any discrepancies in a digital log</span>
  </li>
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>If a defect is identified, the agent photographs the issue and submits a photo‑based report to the operations team for immediate resolution</span>
  </li>
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>This step ensures that any damage incurred during transit is documented before the customer signs off</span>
  </li>
</ul>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Odometer Verification Against the LR Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The odometer reading on the motorcycle must match the mileage listed on the LR (Logistics Receipt) bilty. The driver reads the mileage, records it in the handover sheet, and cross‑checks it with the bilty. A discrepancy of more than two miles triggers a secondary audit: the driver must present a second reading and a brief explanation.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>Once verified, the mileage is stamped on the bilty and the handover sheet, confirming that the vehicle was delivered with the correct mileage</span>
  </li>
</ul>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Signed Condition Sign‑Off</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">After the visual and mileage checks are complete, the customer’s representative signs the delivery sheet. The signature confirms that the motorcycle was delivered in the condition documented and that the odometer reading is accurate. The delivery team signs the same sheet, attaching the driver’s ID and the date.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>Both parties retain copies of the signed sheet and any attached photos for future reference</span>
  </li>
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>This signed condition sign‑off is the final legal acknowledgment that the motorcycle has been received in the agreed state</span>
  </li>
</ul>
  </div>
</div>

<p>By adhering to this structured handover process—daylight re‑inspection, odometer verification, and signed condition sign‑off—companies can protect themselves from post‑delivery disputes, maintain customer trust, and uphold the integrity of their logistics operations.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



